    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d11">

                <pb facs="0104" n="36" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg36"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1885.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-12-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 10, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 23d of November, No.
                    1275, is received and approved. In regard to our claims on the ground of
                    violations of neutrality, I think the President’s message well expresses the
                    sense and the feelings of Congress and the people of the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chales Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
